{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Please come through. I'll just check the pressure before doctor calls you in.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Thank you. Traffic from Koramangala was mad, forty minutes for a small distance only.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Bangalore traffic, what to do. Arm straight please.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Even the auto fellow was grumbling. Doctor is running late, no?",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): A little only. Pressure is 128 over 82, pulse 76. I have put it on the screen.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): 128 is okay, no? My home machine last time showed some other number, I forget.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Doctor will see that. Kindly sit inside, he is fighting with the computer.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sorry, err, one second, this screen has hung. Right. What is the problem today?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Doctor, umm, bloating and loose motions. Whenever I take milk or ice cream.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): Say again please, I clicked the wrong place.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Bloating, and loose motions after milk and ice cream. It's been four months now. Only after dairy, then two or three loose motions, and the stomach is like a balloon.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sorry, and the milk, how much in a day? I was reading the old note.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): Morning chai I cannot leave, three cups, all with milk. Ice cream is extra, that one is worse.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any weight loss in these four months?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Not really. Saree fitting is the same.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (DOCTOR): Blood in the motion?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Never. I would have come running only.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): Fever?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): No fever.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): The bloating, is it painful, or just fullness?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): Not painful. Just the bloating, then loose stools.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): You tried leaving the dairy?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): I tried for one week. No milk, no ice cream. Bloating was much less. Then I had ice cream and the same night the loose motions came back.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): It was my grandson's birthday at the club. He turned seven. India was playing Australia, Kohli was batting, we were all shouting. Kohli got out on 42, very sad, then the rain started, proper heavy rain, cake melting, traffic back was worse than Koramangala.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (DOCTOR): Right. Sorry, a warning popped up, I lost the last part. Leave the match. What happened with the milk, say again.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): One week I avoided dairy and I was better. Ice cream once, loose motions the same night. Nothing else.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): Vomiting?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Not even once.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): Anything else, waterworks, joints, skin, all fine?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Waterworks is fine. Joints also fine. Skin I am not having any problem.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): I see hypertension in the old notes. Still there?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, BP is there since many years. I take, uh, amlodipin for it.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): Dose? The screen jumped, say again.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Amlodipin 5 mg, one tablet every morning.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any chest pain with the BP?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Nothing like that.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): Headaches?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. If I skip the tablet, or the heat is too much, a little headache comes.",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): Swelling of the feet?",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (DOCTOR): Breathlessness?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really.",
  "[SEG0043] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any allergy, medicines or food?",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): No, nothing.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (DOCTOR): Family side, stomach problems, coeliac, anyone?",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): My sister has coeliac. They found it in Mumbai last year. I remembered just now only.",
  "[SEG0047] person_3 (DOCTOR): Hmm. I was going to book a hydrogen breath test for lactose, next Tuesday, in the lab.",
  "[SEG0048] person_3 (DOCTOR): Actually scratch that. With your sister, most likely this is lactose intolerance, but I cannot rule out coeliac.",
  "[SEG0049] person_3 (DOCTOR): We will do the coeliac blood test first. Come Thursday morning, fasting, nothing from midnight, and take the amlodipin only after the blood is drawn. If those are borderline we do the endomysial antibody. If the loose motions do not settle, then a scan.",
  "[SEG0050] person_3 (DOCTOR): Kindly keep a diet diary these two weeks, food and the bloating. I'll see you in two weeks with the report. Keep the dairy low till then.",
  "[SEG0051] person_2 (PATIENT): Thursday fasting, diary, two weeks. My daughter will write the diary, my handwriting is hopeless.",
  "[SEG0052] person_3 (DOCTOR): That is fine. Tummy is soft, no tenderness when I press.",
  "[SEG0053] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Thursday 8.30 morning, blood room, your name is in. No food from midnight, tablet after they draw, same as doctor said.",
  "[SEG0054] person_2 (PATIENT): 8.30, fasting, I will be there. Thank you doctor."
 ],
